From d817529cc99dd1210fe2b03dd84818cfe2784cbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:54:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(tools): close the three mesh-body review blockers

- A spindle body grows by its pad at both axial ends of every band, so
  an internal shoulder grows along the axis too; the outline is the
  union of the grown bands and the safety check reads the grown bands.
- An assembled lathe tool keeps its pad: the lathe body holds it, every
  rebuild keeps it, and the tool body on file writes an optional strict
  `pad` key, so save and open give the same bands.
- A stated mounting frame, port or CIP that the STEP reader refused
  refuses the body by name; it is never read as absent.

Refs #3643

